BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the internal execution workflow of Python programs. Compare CPython with compiled languages \(C/C++\) and explain the roles of Bytecode and the Python Virtual Machine \(PVM\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Architecture of CPython Execution:) Tj
T*
(   Python is traditionally classified as an interpreted language, but modern CPython employs a) Tj
T*
(   two-tier compilation-interpretation pipeline:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Source Code \(.py\) -> Parser & AST Generator: The Lexer tokenizes the source text and) Tj
T*
(   constructs an Abstract Syntax Tree \(AST\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: AST -> Bytecode \(.pyc\): The compiler translates AST nodes into low-level,) Tj
T*
(   platform-independent instruction sequences called Bytecode. Bytecode files are cached inside) Tj
T*
(   the __pycache__ directory with .pyc extensions to accelerate subsequent startup times.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Bytecode -> Python Virtual Machine \(PVM\): The PVM is a stack-based virtual machine) Tj
T*
(   written in C. It iterates through the bytecode instruction loop \(the evaluation loop,) Tj
T*
(   PyEval_EvalFrameDefault\), decoding each opcode and executing the corresponding C library) Tj
T*
(   routine.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparison with Purely Compiled Languages \(C/C++\):) Tj
T*
(   - Compilation Target: C/C++ compiles source code directly to hardware-specific machine code) Tj
T*
(   binaries \(.exe, ELF\) via GCC/Clang. Python compiles to abstract intermediate bytecode.) Tj
T*
(   - Portability: Python bytecode can execute on any operating system equipped with a compatible) Tj
T*
(   PVM. C binaries are strictly bound to target CPU architectures and OS ABIs.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution Speed: C executes directly on bare silicon with zero runtime interpreter overhead.) Tj
T*
(   Python incurs interpretive dispatch overhead, dynamic type checking, and boxing/unboxing costs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Working Python Demonstration \(Bytecode Disassembly\):) Tj
T*
(   import dis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def compute_kinetic_energy\(mass, velocity\):) Tj
T*
(   '''Calculate kinetic energy: 0.5 * m * v^2''') Tj
T*
(   energy = 0.5 * mass * \(velocity ** 2\)) Tj
T*
(   return energy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Disassembled Bytecode for compute_kinetic_energy:"\)) Tj
T*
(   dis.dis\(compute_kinetic_energy\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model & Execution Trace:) Tj
T*
(   - When compute_kinetic_energy\(10, 5\) is invoked:) Tj
T*
(   Stack Frame: Pushed onto PVM call stack.) Tj
T*
(   Local Symbol Table: {'mass': 10, 'velocity': 5, 'energy': 125.0}.) Tj
T*
(   Operand Stack Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   LOAD_CONST 0.5 -> Push 0.5) Tj
T*
(   LOAD_FAST mass \(10\) -> Push 10) Tj
T*
(   BINARY_MULTIPLY -> Pop both, compute 5.0, push 5.0) Tj
T*
(   LOAD_FAST velocity \(5\) -> Push 5) Tj
T*
(   LOAD_CONST 2 -> Push 2) Tj
T*
(   BINARY_POWER -> Pop both, compute 25, push 25) Tj
T*
(   BINARY_MULTIPLY -> Pop 5.0 and 25, compute 125.0, push 125.0) Tj
T*
(   STORE_FAST energy -> Store top of stack into local variable 'energy') Tj
T*
(   LOAD_FAST energy -> Push 125.0) Tj
T*
(   RETURN_VALUE -> Return 125.0 and pop stack frame.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
