BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss Python's Object Model and Dynamic Typing. Explain the three fundamental attributes of every Python object \(Identity, Type, Value\) with code demonstrations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundation of Python's Object Model:) Tj
T*
(   In Python, 'everything is a first-class object' - functions, modules, primitive numbers, and) Tj
T*
(   classes are all instances of PyObject in CPython heap memory.) Tj
T*
(   Every object in Python is defined by three immutable pillars:) Tj
T*
(   1. Identity: The unique physical or virtual memory address where the object resides. Inspected) Tj
T*
(   via id\(obj\). In CPython, id\(obj\) returns the actual pointer address cast to an integer.) Tj
T*
(   2. Type: Defines the set of possible values, valid operations, and methods supported by the) Tj
T*
(   object. Inspected via type\(obj\). An object's type cannot be changed after instantiation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Value: The actual data or state payload stored within the object's allocated memory block.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dynamic Typing vs Static Typing:) Tj
T*
(   - In statically-typed languages \(Java/C++\), variables are named containers of a fixed type: int) Tj
T*
(   x = 10;) Tj
T*
(   - In Python, variables are purely symbolic name tags \(references or pointers\) bound to objects) Tj
T*
(   residing on the heap: x = 10. The name 'x' has no type; the integer object 10 possesses the) Tj
T*
(   type 'int'. Rebinding x = 'Hello' merely points the name 'x' to a newly allocated string) Tj
T*
(   object.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation & Verification:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def inspect_object\(name, obj\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Name: {name:<8} | Type: {type\(obj\).__name__:<10} | ID: {id\(obj\)} | Size:) Tj
T*
(   {sys.getsizeof\(obj\)} bytes | Value: {repr\(obj\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   val = 42) Tj
T*
(   inspect_object\("val", val\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   val = "Python Dynamic Typing") Tj
T*
(   inspect_object\("val", val\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   val = [10, 20, 30]) Tj
T*
(   inspect_object\("val", val\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model & Reference Binding Trace:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: val = 42 -> An int object with ob_refcnt=1, ob_type=&PyLong_Type, ob_digit=[42] is) Tj
T*
(   allocated on the heap. 'val' in globals\(\) dict points to this address.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: val = 'Python Dynamic Typing' -> A new PyUnicodeObject is allocated. 'val' pointer is) Tj
T*
(   redirected to the string object. The integer 42's reference count is decremented.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: val = [10, 20, 30] -> A PyListObject containing an array of three pointers to) Tj
T*
(   integers is allocated. 'val' is rebound. The string's reference count drops to 0 and its memory) Tj
T*
(   is reclaimed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) for type lookup, identity retrieval, and variable rebinding.) Tj
T*
ET

