(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain CPython's Small Integer Caching \(-5 to 256\) and String Interning mechanisms. Write code to verify memory identity \(is\) versus value equality \(==\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Memory Optimization via Caching and Interning:) Tj
T*
(   CPython incorporates specific memory and runtime optimizations to mitigate dynamic allocation) Tj
T*
(   overhead for frequently used immutable entities:) Tj
T*
(   - Small Integer Caching: Upon interpreter startup, CPython allocates an internal array of 262) Tj
T*
(   integer objects covering the inclusive range [-5, 256]. Any arithmetic operation or assignment) Tj
T*
(   yielding an integer in this range binds to the pre-existing singleton object, avoiding repeated) Tj
T*
(   heap allocations.) Tj
T*
(   - String Interning: Immutable strings that look like valid identifiers \(alphanumeric with) Tj
T*
(   underscores\) are automatically 'interned' into an internal dictionary. When interned, Python) Tj
T*
(   verifies string equality in O\(1\) pointer comparison \(is\) rather than O\(N\)) Tj
T*
(   character-by-character scanning \(==\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Identity \('is'\) vs Equality \('=='\):) Tj
T*
(   - Operator '==': Evaluates the __eq__\(\) method to determine whether two objects have equivalent) Tj
T*
(   content/values.) Tj
T*
(   - Operator 'is': Evaluates pointer identity: id\(a\) == id\(b\). It tests whether both names point) Tj
T*
(   to the exact same physical heap memory buffer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Demonstration Code:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Test 1: Small Integer Caching \(-5 to 256\)) Tj
T*
(   x1 = 250 + 6 # 256) Tj
T*
(   y1 = 256) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"256 -> Equality: {x1 == y1}, Identity: {x1 is y1}, id\(x1\): {id\(x1\)}, id\(y1\): {id\(y1\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   x2 = 257) Tj
T*
(   y2 = 257) Tj
T*
(   # In REPL, x2 and y2 will have different IDs; in compiled code block they may be co-allocated) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"257 -> Equality: {x2 == y2}, Identity: {x2 is y2}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Test 2: String Interning) Tj
T*
(   str1 = "python_identifier") Tj
T*
(   str2 = "python_identifier") Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Interned Strings -> str1 is str2: {str1 is str2}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Explicit Interning using sys.intern\(\)) Tj
T*
(   dyn1 = sys.intern\("hello world!" + ""\)) Tj
T*
(   dyn2 = sys.intern\("hello world!" + ""\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Explicitly Interned -> dyn1 is dyn2: {dyn1 is dyn2}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model Diagram / Trace:) Tj
T*
(   Global Namespace:) Tj
T*
(   [x1] -------------> [ PyLongObject: 256 ] <------------- [y1] \(Shared Singleton in small_ints) Tj
T*
(   array\)) Tj
T*
(   [x2] -------------> [ PyLongObject: 257 at 0x7f8a1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [y2] -------------> [ PyLongObject: 257 at 0x7f8b4 ] \(Distinct Heap Allocations\)) Tj
T*
ET

