(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Mutable vs Immutable data types in Python. Detail how memory allocation behaves during in-place mutations vs rebinding operations with illustrative code.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mutability Concept in Python:) Tj
T*
(   Python classifies all data types into two distinct categories:) Tj
T*
(   - Immutable Types: Objects whose internal memory representation and state cannot be modified) Tj
T*
(   after creation. Examples: int, float, complex, bool, str, tuple, frozenset, bytes.) Tj
T*
(   When an 'alteration' is performed on an immutable object, Python does NOT modify the object; it) Tj
T*
(   allocates a brand new object on the heap and rebinds the variable reference.) Tj
T*
(   - Mutable Types: Objects whose internal content can be modified in-place without altering the) Tj
T*
(   object's identity or memory address. Examples: list, dict, set, bytearray.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Behavioral Differences & Memory Implications:) Tj
T*
(   Modifying a mutable object alters the shared state for all variable references pointing to that) Tj
T*
(   object \(aliasing\). In contrast, rebinding an immutable variable affects only the local) Tj
T*
(   reference.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   # Part A: Immutable Type \(int & str\)) Tj
T*
(   num = 50) Tj
T*
(   initial_id = id\(num\)) Tj
T*
(   num += 5) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Immutable Int: Initial ID = {initial_id}, Post-Addition ID = {id\(num\)} \(Different) Tj
T*
(   Object Allocated!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   greeting = "Hello") Tj
T*
(   g_id = id\(greeting\)) Tj
T*
(   greeting += " World") Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Immutable String: Initial ID = {g_id}, Post-Concat ID = {id\(greeting\)} \(Different) Tj
T*
(   Object Allocated!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Part B: Mutable Type \(list\)) Tj
T*
(   my_list = [10, 20, 30]) Tj
T*
(   list_id = id\(my_list\)) Tj
T*
(   my_list.append\(40\)) Tj
T*
(   my_list[0] = 99) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Mutable List: Initial ID = {list_id}, Post-Mutation ID = {id\(my_list\)} \(Same Memory) Tj
T*
(   Address!\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Updated List Content: {my_list}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model Trace:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Immutable\):) Tj
T*
(   Stack: num -> Heap 0x1000 [int: 50]) Tj
T*
(   num += 5 -> Allocates Heap 0x1040 [int: 55]. Stack: num -> 0x1040. Heap 0x1000 refcount) Tj
T*
(   decrements.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Mutable\):) Tj
T*
