(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Python's Arithmetic Operators \(+, -, *, /, //, %, **\). Explain Floor Division \(//\) and Modulus \(%\) with positive and negative operands.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Comprehensive Inventory of Arithmetic Operators:) Tj
T*
(   - Addition \(+\), Subtraction \(-\), Multiplication \(*\).) Tj
T*
(   - True Division \(/\): Always returns a float in Python 3, even if operands divide evenly \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   4 / 2 -> 2.0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Floor Division \(//\): Divides operands and truncates the quotient to the nearest mathematical) Tj
T*
(   floor integer \(i.e., floor\(a / b\) = greatest integer <= a / b\).) Tj
T*
(   - Modulus \(%\): Returns remainder r satisfying the fundamental mathematical identity:) Tj
T*
(   a = \(b * \(a // b\)\) + \(a % b\)) Tj
T*
(   Consequently: a % b = a - b * \(a // b\).) Tj
T*
(   Notice: The sign of \(a % b\) in Python always matches the sign of the divisor b.) Tj
T*
(   - Exponentiation \(**\): Computes power with right-to-left associativity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Breakdown for Floor Division and Modulus:) Tj
T*
(   Case 1: 7 // 3 = 2, 7 % 3 = 7 - 3 * 2 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Case 2: -7 // 3 = -3 \(since -7 / 3 = -2.333; floor\(-2.333\) = -3\).) Tj
T*
(   -7 % 3 = -7 - 3 * \(-3\) = -7 + 9 = 2.) Tj
T*
(   Case 3: 7 // -3 = -3.) Tj
T*
(   7 % -3 = 7 - \(-3\) * \(-3\) = 7 - 9 = -2.) Tj
T*
(   Case 4: -7 // -3 = 2.) Tj
T*
(   -7 % -3 = -7 - \(-3\) * 2 = -7 + 6 = -1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Verification Program:) Tj
T*
(   def verify_division_identity\(a, b\):) Tj
T*
(   quotient = a // b) Tj
T*
(   remainder = a % b) Tj
T*
(   identity_check = \(b * quotient\) + remainder == a) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"a = {a:2}, b = {b:2} | a // b = {quotient:2} | a % b = {remainder:2} | Identity Holds:) Tj
T*
(   {identity_check}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Verification of Python Arithmetic Identity: a = \(b * \(a // b\)\) + \(a % b\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   verify_division_identity\(7, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   verify_division_identity\(-7, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   verify_division_identity\(7, -3\)) Tj
T*
(   verify_division_identity\(-7, -3\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) for fixed-width integers; O\(M * N\) for arbitrary precision Karatsuba /) Tj
T*
(   schoolbook division on massive integers.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) storage for result.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
