(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Operator Precedence and Associativity in Python. Provide a full hierarchy table from highest to lowest precedence with illustrative evaluation examples.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Precedence and Associativity Principles:) Tj
T*
(   Operator Precedence dictates the binding priority of operators in an unparenthesized compound) Tj
T*
(   expression. Operators with higher precedence are evaluated before operators with lower) Tj
T*
(   precedence.) Tj
T*
(   Associativity determines the evaluation direction \(Left-to-Right vs Right-to-Left\) when) Tj
T*
(   operators of identical precedence appear consecutively.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete Python Operator Precedence Hierarchy \(Highest to Lowest\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Parentheses: \( \) - Highest binding) Tj
T*
(   2. Exponentiation: ** \(Right-to-Left associativity: 2**3**2 = 2**9 = 512\)) Tj
T*
(   3. Unary Operators: +x, -x, ~x \(Positive, Negative, Bitwise NOT\)) Tj
T*
(   4. Multiplicative: *, /, //, % \(Left-to-Right\)) Tj
T*
(   5. Additive: +, - \(Left-to-Right\)) Tj
T*
(   6. Bitwise Shifts: <<, >>) Tj
T*
(   7. Bitwise AND: &) Tj
T*
(   8. Bitwise XOR: ^) Tj
T*
(   9. Bitwise OR: |) Tj
T*
(   10. Comparison, Identity & Membership: ==, !=, <, <=, >, >=, is, is not, in, not in) Tj
T*
(   11. Boolean NOT: not) Tj
T*
(   12. Boolean AND: and) Tj
T*
(   13. Boolean OR: or) Tj
T*
(   14. Conditional Expression: x if condition else y) Tj
T*
(   15. Assignment & Walrus: =, +=, -=, *=, /=, := - Lowest) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Expression Evaluation Trace:) Tj
T*
(   Expression: result = 10 + 2 * 3 ** 2 > 25 and not 4 & 1 == 0) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Exponentiation: 3 ** 2 -> 9) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Multiplication: 2 * 9 -> 18) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Addition: 10 + 18 -> 28) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Comparison 1: 28 > 25 -> True) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Bitwise AND: 4 & 1 -> 0 \(binary 100 & 001 = 000\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Comparison 2: 0 == 0 -> True) Tj
T*
(   Step 7: Logical NOT: not True -> False) Tj
T*
(   Step 8: Logical AND: True and False -> False) Tj
T*
(   Final Value: False) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   expr_val = 10 + 2 * 3 ** 2 > 25 and not 4 & 1 == 0) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Evaluated Compound Expression: {expr_val}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstrating Right-to-Left Associativity of Exponentiation) Tj
T*
(   rtl_power = 2 ** 3 ** 2) Tj
T*
(   ltr_equiv = 2 ** \(3 ** 2\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"2 ** 3 ** 2 = {rtl_power} \(Matches Right-to-Left: {rtl_power == ltr_equiv}\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) arithmetic and logical evaluations.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) temporary values on PVM evaluation stack.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

