(   - Bitwise NOT \(~\): Inverts all bits.) Tj
T*
(   - Left Shift \(<<\): Shifts bits left by n positions, equivalent to multiplying by 2^n: x << n =) Tj
T*
(   x * \(2**n\).) Tj
T*
(   - Right Shift \(>>\): Shifts bits right by n positions, equivalent to floor dividing by 2^n: x >>) Tj
T*
(   n = x // \(2**n\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Two's Complement Arithmetic & The ~x Identity:) Tj
T*
(   In computer systems, negative integers are represented using two's complement notation:) Tj
T*
(   - For any integer x, its two's complement negative representation -x is obtained by inverting) Tj
T*
(   all bits \(~x\) and adding 1:) Tj
T*
(   -x = ~x + 1) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging this fundamental formula algebraically:) Tj
T*
(   ~x = -x - 1 = -\(x + 1\)) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   ~0 = -\(0 + 1\) = -1) Tj
T*
(   ~5 = -\(5 + 1\) = -6) Tj
T*
(   ~\(-8\) = -\(-8 + 1\) = 7) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation & Bitwise Flag Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   # Permissions System Using Bitwise Flags) Tj
T*
(   READ = 1 << 0 # 0001 \(1\)) Tj
T*
(   WRITE = 1 << 1 # 0010 \(2\)) Tj
T*
(   EXECUTE = 1 << 2 # 0100 \(4\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   user_perm = READ | WRITE # 0011 \(3\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def check_permission\(perm, flag\):) Tj
T*
(   return \(perm & flag\) != 0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"User Permissions: bin={bin\(user_perm\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Has Read Access: {check_permission\(user_perm, READ\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Has Execute Access: {check_permission\(user_perm, EXECUTE\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Bitwise Shifts) Tj
T*
(   val = 12) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"12 << 2 = {val << 2} \(12 * 4\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"12 >> 2 = {val >> 2} \(12 // 4\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"~12 = {~val} \(Formula: -\(12 + 1\) = -13\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) for machine word bitwise operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) integer registers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
