(   [Problem Statement]: Explain String Indexing and Slicing in Python. Detail the syntax s[start:stop:step], positive vs negative indexing, boundary defaults, and slice reversal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. String Structure as an Ordered Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   In Python, strings \(str\) are immutable ordered sequences of Unicode code points. Characters are) Tj
T*
(   indexed starting from 0 up to len\(s\) - 1. Python also supports negative indexing from -1 \(last) Tj
T*
(   character\) down to -len\(s\) \(first character\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Slicing Syntax: s[start : stop : step]) Tj
T*
