() Tj
T*
(   3. Special Slicing Patterns:) Tj
T*
(   - s[:] -> Creates a shallow copy of the entire string.) Tj
T*
(   - s[::2] -> Extracts every second character \(even indices\).) Tj
T*
(   - s[1::2] -> Extracts characters at odd indices.) Tj
T*
(   - s[::-1] -> Traverses the string in reverse direction, producing a reversed string.) Tj
T*
(   - Boundary Handling: Slicing never raises an IndexError even if indices exceed string) Tj
T*
(   boundaries; Python automatically clamps indices to [0, len\(s\)].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   text = "ComputerScience") Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original String: '{text}' \(Length: {len\(text\)}\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Positive Indexing & Slicing) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[0:8] -> '{text[0:8]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[8:] -> '{text[8:]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[::2] -> '{text[::2]}'"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Negative Indexing & Slicing) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[-7:] -> '{text[-7:]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[:-7] -> '{text[:-7]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[::-1] -> '{text[::-1]}' \(Reversed\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Boundary Clamping Tolerance) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"text[5:100] -> '{text[5:100]}' \(No IndexError raised\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(K\) where K = len\(slice\) is the number of characters extracted to create) Tj
T*
(   the new string.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(K\) memory allocated for the new sliced string object.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
