12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Python Standard Library and the 'Batteries Included' philosophy. Provide examples of 5 essential built-in modules \(math, sys, os, random, time\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Python's 'Batteries Included' Philosophy:) Tj
T*
(   Conceived by Guido van Rossum, 'Batteries Included' means Python ships with a comprehensive,) Tj
T*
(   robust standard library out of the box. Developers can build networking services, parse) Tj
T*
(   CSV/JSON, calculate statistical distributions, and interact with operating systems without) Tj
T*
(   needing third-party dependencies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Deep Dive into 5 Essential Standard Library Modules:) Tj
T*
(   1. math: C-standard mathematical functions \(trigonometric, logarithmic, gamma, constants pi and) Tj
T*
(   e\).) Tj
T*
(   2. sys: System-specific parameters and interpreter controls \(sys.argv, sys.path, sys.version,) Tj
T*
(   sys.exit\).) Tj
T*
(   3. os: Operating system interface \(file management, directories, environment variables) Tj
T*
(   os.environ\).) Tj
T*
(   4. random: Pseudo-random number generator implementing the Mersenne Twister algorithm \(PRNG\).) Tj
T*
(   5. time: Wall-clock time, CPU execution timers, and sleep pauses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Integrated Python Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
(   import os) Tj
T*
(   import random) Tj
T*
(   import time) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. math demonstration) Tj
T*
(   hypot = math.hypot\(3, 4\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"math.hypot\(3, 4\) = {hypot} | math.pi = {math.pi:.4f}"\)) Tj
T*
