12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain CPython's Reference Counting and Cyclic Garbage Collection mechanisms. How are reference cycles detected and resolved?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Dual Memory Management Architecture in CPython:) Tj
T*
(   Memory reclamation in CPython relies on two cooperating systems:) Tj
T*
(   System 1: Reference Counting \(Primary, Real-Time\):) Tj
T*
(   Every PyObject contains an internal field ob_refcnt. Whenever a new variable references the) Tj
T*
(   object, its reference count increments. Whenever a reference goes out of scope or is deleted) Tj
T*
(   \(del var\), the count decrements. When ob_refcnt == 0, the object is immediately deallocated and) Tj
T*
(   its memory freed back to the pymalloc allocator.) Tj
T*
(   System 2: Cyclic Generational Garbage Collector \(Secondary, Periodic\):) Tj
T*
(   Reference counting alone fails when objects reference each other cyclically \(e.g., node_a.next) Tj
T*
(   = node_b and node_b.prev = node_a\). Even if the user deletes external references to node_a and) Tj
T*
(   node_b, their internal reference counts remain at 1, causing a permanent memory leak. The) Tj
T*
(   cyclic GC identifies and collects these isolated circular islands.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Generational GC Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   CPython categorizes objects into three generations \(Gen 0, Gen 1, Gen 2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 0: Holds newly allocated objects. Collected most frequently.) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 1 & 2: Objects that survive collections are promoted to older generations and scanned) Tj
T*
(   less frequently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import gc) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class CycleNode:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, name\):) Tj
T*
(   self.name = name) Tj
T*
(   self.link = None) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Create isolated circular reference) Tj
T*
(   node_a = CycleNode\("A"\)) Tj
T*
(   node_b = CycleNode\("B"\)) Tj
T*
(   node_a.link = node_b) Tj
T*
(   node_b.link = node_a) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Break external variable references) Tj
T*
(   del node_a) Tj
T*
(   del node_b) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("External references deleted, circular reference trapped in heap."\)) Tj
T*
(   # Manually trigger cyclic garbage collection) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
