(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python's sys.argv and Command-Line Argument Processing. Write a standalone Python script demonstrating command-line parameter parsing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Command-Line Execution:) Tj
T*
(   When a Python script is launched from the Windows command line or PowerShell \(e.g., python) Tj
T*
(   process.py input.csv --verbose\), the arguments passed to the script are captured by the runtime) Tj
T*
(   and exposed as a list of strings in the sys module: sys.argv.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structure of sys.argv:) Tj
T*
(   - sys.argv[0]: The script filename or path being executed.) Tj
T*
(   - sys.argv[1:]: The actual positional parameters and flags passed by the user.) Tj
T*
(   - All items in sys.argv are strictly strings \(str\); numeric parameters must be explicitly) Tj
T*
(   converted using int\(\) or float\(\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Robust Python Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def parse_cli_arguments\(args\):) Tj
T*
(   """Simulate command-line argument processing.""") Tj
T*
(   if len\(args\) < 3:) Tj
T*
(   return "Usage: python script.py <operation: add|mul> <num1> <num2>") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   op = args[1].lower\(\)) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   n1 = float\(args[2]\)) Tj
T*
(   n2 = float\(args[3]\)) Tj
T*
(   except ValueError:) Tj
T*
(   return "Error: Both arguments must be valid numeric numbers.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if op == "add":) Tj
T*
(   return f"Result of {n1} + {n2} = {n1 + n2}") Tj
T*
(   elif op == "mul":) Tj
T*
(   return f"Result of {n1} * {n2} = {n1 * n2}") Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   return f"Error: Unknown operation '{op}'. Supported: add, mul.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Simulation with mock command line arguments) Tj
T*
(   mock_args = ["calc.py", "mul", "12.5", "4"]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Simulating command: {' '.join\(mock_args\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   result = parse_cli_arguments\(mock_args\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(result\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) argument indexing and validation.) Tj
T*
ET

