BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Floating-Point Representation \(IEEE 754\) in Python. Why does 0.1 + 0.2 != 0.3, and how should financial/scientific calculations handle precision?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Binary Floating-Point Representation:) Tj
T*
(   Python's float type is implemented as a 64-bit double precision value conforming to IEEE 754) Tj
T*
(   standard:) Tj
T*
(   - 1 sign bit) Tj
T*
(   - 11 exponent bits) Tj
T*
(   - 52 fraction \(mantissa\) bits \(yielding ~15 to 17 significant decimal digits of precision\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Why 0.1 + 0.2 != 0.3:) Tj
T*
(   In base-10, numbers like 1/3 cannot be represented with finite decimal digits \(0.3333...\).) Tj
T*
(   Similarly, in base-2 \(binary\), numbers like 0.1 \(1/10\) and 0.2 \(1/5\) result in infinitely) Tj
T*
(   repeating binary fractions:) Tj
T*
(   - 0.1 in binary = 0.0001100110011001100110011...) Tj
T*
(   When stored in 53 bits of precision, the number must be rounded. When 0.1 and 0.2 are added in) Tj
T*
(   binary:) Tj
T*
(   0.1 + 0.2 = 0.300000000000000044408920985006...) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, the equality test 0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3 evaluates to False!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Industry Solutions for Exact Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   1. For Scientific Calculations: Use math.isclose\(a, b, rel_tol=1e-9\) to check equality within a) Tj
T*
(   tolerance epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   2. For Financial/Banking Calculations: Use the decimal.Decimal class, which implements exact) Tj
T*
(   base-10 fixed-point arithmetic without binary representation errors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
(   from decimal import Decimal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # IEEE 754 Error Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   sum_float = 0.1 + 0.2) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"0.1 + 0.2 = {sum_float:.20f}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3 -> {sum_float == 0.3}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Solution 1: math.isclose\(\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"math.isclose\(0.1 + 0.2, 0.3\) -> {math.isclose\(sum_float, 0.3\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Solution 2: decimal.Decimal) Tj
T*
(   dec1 = Decimal\('0.1'\)) Tj
T*
(   dec2 = Decimal\('0.2'\)) Tj
T*
(   dec_sum = dec1 + dec2) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Decimal\('0.1'\) + Decimal\('0.2'\) = {dec_sum} \(Exact Match: {dec_sum ==) Tj
T*
(   Decimal\('0.3'\)}\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Float Operations: O\(1\) hardware CPU ALU execution.) Tj
T*
(   - Decimal Operations: O\(D\) software emulation arithmetic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
