(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   Engineering applications frequently require seamless conversion across thermodynamic) Tj
T*
(   temperature scales: Celsius \(C\), Fahrenheit \(F\), and Kelvin \(K\). The program must validate) Tj
T*
(   inputs \(e.g., rejecting temperatures below Absolute Zero: -273.15 C or 0 K\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Thermodynamic Formulas:) Tj
T*
(   - F = \(C * 9/5\) + 32) Tj
T*
(   - C = \(F - 32\) * 5/9) Tj
T*
(   - K = C + 273.15) Tj
T*
(   - C = K - 273.15) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class TemperatureConverter:) Tj
T*
(   ABSOLUTE_ZERO_C = -273.15) Tj
T*
(   ABSOLUTE_ZERO_K = 0.0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @staticmethod) Tj
T*
(   def celsius_to_all\(celsius: float\):) Tj
T*
(   if celsius < TemperatureConverter.ABSOLUTE_ZERO_C:) Tj
T*
(   raise ValueError\(f"Physics Violation: Temperature {celsius} C is below Absolute Zero \(-273.15) Tj
T*
(   C\)!"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   fahrenheit = \(celsius * 9 / 5\) + 32) Tj
T*
(   kelvin = celsius + 273.15) Tj
T*
(   return {"Celsius": celsius, "Fahrenheit": round\(fahrenheit, 2\), "Kelvin": round\(kelvin, 2\)}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @staticmethod) Tj
T*
(   def fahrenheit_to_all\(fahrenheit: float\):) Tj
T*
(   celsius = \(fahrenheit - 32\) * 5 / 9) Tj
T*
(   return TemperatureConverter.celsius_to_all\(celsius\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration and Verification) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   c_sample = 37.0 # Human body temperature) Tj
T*
(   res = TemperatureConverter.celsius_to_all\(c_sample\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Human Body Temp: {res['Celsius']} C = {res['Fahrenheit']} F = {res['Kelvin']} K"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Boundary test: Absolute zero) Tj
T*
(   abs_zero = TemperatureConverter.celsius_to_all\(-273.15\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Absolute Zero: {abs_zero['Celsius']} C = {abs_zero['Fahrenheit']} F =) Tj
T*
(   {abs_zero['Kelvin']} K"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Invalid temperature test) Tj
T*
(   TemperatureConverter.celsius_to_all\(-300.0\)) Tj
T*
(   except ValueError as err:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Validation Caught: {err}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model & Complexity:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) elementary arithmetic operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) dictionary creation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
