12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain String Encoding and Decoding \(ASCII, UTF-8, Unicode\) in Python. Detail how str.encode\(\) and bytes.decode\(\) bridge text and binary data.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Need for Character Encodings:) Tj
T*
(   Computers store bytes \(8-bit sequences of 0s and 1s\). Human languages use abstract symbols) Tj
T*
(   \(letters, ideograms, emojis\). An encoding is a translation mapping between abstract character) Tj
T*
(   code points and concrete byte sequences:) Tj
T*
(   - ASCII: 7-bit encoding supporting 128 English characters \(0x00 to 0x7F\).) Tj
T*
(   - Unicode: A universal character set mapping over 149,000 characters from all world languages) Tj
T*
(   to integer code points \(U+0000 to U+10FFFF\).) Tj
T*
(   - UTF-8: A variable-length encoding \(1 to 4 bytes per code point\). It is backward compatible) Tj
T*
(   with 7-bit ASCII and is the dominant encoding standard of the World Wide Web.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Bridging str and bytes in Python:) Tj
T*
(   - str: An abstract sequence of Unicode code points. Human-readable text.) Tj
T*
(   - bytes: An immutable sequence of raw 8-bit integers \(0 to 255\). Machine/network readable.) Tj
T*
(   - encode\('utf-8'\): Translates str -> bytes.) Tj
T*
(   - decode\('utf-8'\): Translates bytes -> str.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Demonstration Code:) Tj
T*
(   # Original Unicode String with Multilingual Content) Tj
T*
(   text = "Python ? CSE \(?\)" # Heart and Greek Pi) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original Text \(str\): {text} \(Length: {len\(text\)} characters\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Encoding to UTF-8 Bytes) Tj
T*
(   utf8_bytes = text.encode\('utf-8'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"UTF-8 Encoded \(bytes\): {utf8_bytes} \(Length: {len\(utf8_bytes\)} bytes\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Decoding back to Unicode String) Tj
T*
(   restored_text = utf8_bytes.decode\('utf-8'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Decoded Text Matches: {restored_text == text}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Error Handling Strategies during Decoding) Tj
T*
(   corrupt_bytes = b"Hello ? World") Tj
T*
(   decoded_ignore = corrupt_bytes.decode\('utf-8', errors='ignore'\)) Tj
T*
(   decoded_replace = corrupt_bytes.decode\('utf-8', errors='replace'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Ignore Errors: '{decoded_ignore}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Replace Errors: '{decoded_replace}'"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) where N is string length.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(N\) memory for byte array.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
