(   Python keywords are reserved tokens defined in the interpreter's grammar. They have special) Tj
T*
(   syntactic meaning \(e.g., if, for, class, def, return, yield\) and cannot be assigned as) Tj
T*
(   variable, function, or class names.) Tj
T*
(   Modern Python 3.10+ contains 35 keywords.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dynamic Inspection via keyword Module:) Tj
T*
(   The standard library keyword module provides:) Tj
T*
(   - keyword.kwlist: A sorted list of all reserved keywords.) Tj
T*
(   - keyword.iskeyword\(s\): Returns True if string s is a reserved keyword.) Tj
T*
(   - keyword.issoftkeyword\(s\): Identifies contextual soft keywords introduced in Python 3.10) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., match, case\).) Tj
T*
(   - str.isidentifier\(\): Built-in string method checking if string follows valid identifier) Tj
T*
(   syntax.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation & Identifier Validator:) Tj
T*
(   import keyword) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def validate_python_identifier\(identifier_name: str\) -> tuple:) Tj
T*
(   """Validates whether a string can serve as a legal variable name.""") Tj
T*
(   if not isinstance\(identifier_name, str\):) Tj
T*
(   return \(False, "Identifier must be a string."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if len\(identifier_name\) == 0:) Tj
T*
(   return \(False, "Identifier cannot be empty."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if keyword.iskeyword\(identifier_name\):) Tj
T*
(   return \(False, f"'{identifier_name}' is a reserved Python keyword."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if not identifier_name.isidentifier\(\):) Tj
T*
(   return \(False, f"'{identifier_name}' contains illegal characters or starts with a digit."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return \(True, f"'{identifier_name}' is a completely valid Python identifier."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Test Scenarios) Tj
T*
(   test_cases = ["student_name", "_temp_var", "2nd_rank", "class", "total$sum", "def",) Tj
T*
(   "normalVariable"]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Total Python Keywords: {len\(keyword.kwlist\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("-" * 60\)) Tj
T*
(   for tc in test_cases:) Tj
T*
(   valid, msg = validate_python_identifier\(tc\)) Tj
T*
(   status = "[VALID] " if valid else "[INVALID]") Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{status} {msg}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) hash set lookup in keyword.iskeyword\(\).) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) auxiliary validation overhead.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
