(   \('dunder'\) attributes attached to modules, classes, and instances.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Dunder Attributes:) Tj
T*
(   1. __name__: Holds the name of the module or function. For the main entry script executed) Tj
T*
(   directly, __name__ is set to '__main__'.) Tj
T*
(   2. __doc__: Stores the documentation string \(docstring\) of the entity.) Tj
T*
(   3. __file__: Contains the absolute filesystem path from which the module was loaded.) Tj
T*
(   4. __dict__: A dictionary namespace holding all writable attributes of an object or module.) Tj
T*
(   5. __class__: A reference to the type or class of which the current object is an instance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Demonstration Code:) Tj
T*
(   """Sample Module Docstring for Introspection Demonstration.""") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class StudentProfile:) Tj
T*
(   """Student demographic and academic record class.""") Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, name: str, gpa: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.name = name) Tj
T*
(   self.gpa = gpa) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   stu = StudentProfile\("Meera", 3.88\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Introspecting Module & Object Dunder Attributes:"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Module __name__: {__name__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Class __name__: {StudentProfile.__name__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Class __doc__: {StudentProfile.__doc__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Instance __class__: {stu.__class__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Instance __dict__: {stu.__dict__}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Modifying state through __dict__) Tj
T*
(   stu.__dict__['major'] = 'Computer Science') Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Dynamic Attribute Added via __dict__: stu.major = {stu.major}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Attribute Access: O\(1\) dictionary lookup in instance and class __dict__.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(K\) where K is number of instance attributes stored in __dict__.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
