(   [Problem Statement]: Design an interactive quadratic equation solver in Python that handles real roots, single degenerate roots, and complex conjugate roots with full error handling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   For a quadratic equation a*x^2 + b*x + c = 0 \(where a != 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Discriminant: Delta = b^2 - 4*a*c.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: Delta > 0 -> Two distinct real roots: x = \(-b +/- sqrt\(Delta\)\) / \(2*a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: Delta == 0 -> Single degenerate real root: x = -b / \(2*a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 3: Delta < 0 -> Two complex conjugate roots: x = -b / \(2*a\) +/- \(sqrt\(|Delta|\) / \(2*a\)\)) Tj
T*
(   * 1j.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import cmath) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def solve_quadratic_equation\(a: float, b: float, c: float\):) Tj
T*
ET

